1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,366
Something in your eye?

2
00:00:01,366 --> 00:00:02,025
Don't rub it.

3
00:00:02,025 --> 00:00:02,938
Here's what to do.

4
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:06,260
Step one.

5
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:07,166
Wash your hands.

6
00:00:07,166 --> 00:00:10,337
Don't rub the eye, because that can scratch its surface.

7
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:12,304
Step two.

8
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:13,413
Blink a few times.

9
00:00:13,413 --> 00:00:16,123
Tears often wash the speck out on their own.

10
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:18,425
Step three.

11
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:19,161
Still there?

12
00:00:19,161 --> 00:00:25,110
Rinse with clean, lukewarm water or sterile saline, tilting your head so it runs off to the side.

13
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,298
A speck under the upper lid?

14
00:00:27,298 --> 00:00:31,442
Gently pull the upper lid over the lower one, so the lashes can sweep it away.

15
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:37,174
Don't try to remove anything stuck in the eye, and don't use tweezers or cotton swabs.

16
00:00:37,174 --> 00:00:38,988
Cover it loosely, and get help.

17
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:49,631
Get urgent medical care for a chemical splash, after rinsing for fifteen minutes, or for a stuck object, vision changes, or pain or redness that doesn't go away.
